title: Military Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: military_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and ejercito_minister_party = "SPD" and military_policy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/azana.png
#subtitle: Dealing with the Ejército.

= Military Policy

The Ejército is a deeply reactionary institution, historically prone to *pronunciamientos* and hostility to any notion of liberalism, socialism or social reform of any kind. However, with our party in government and controlling the Ministry of War, we must decide how to handle the military establishment.

- @increase_funding: Increase funding for the military to purchase the loyalty of the officer corps.
- @decrease_funding: Cut military spending to free up funds for social programs.
- @reform: Execute a deep reform of the army, reducing excess officers and ensuring loyalty to the Republic.
- @root: No change to military policy.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@increase_funding
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; ejercito_loyalty += 0.07 if ejercito_loyalty < 1; ejercito_strength += 20; caballeristas_dissent += 5; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; economic_growth += 0.1; ar_relation -= 10;

Conservative generals and right-wing parties are pleasantly surprised that we are expanding military spending. However, our working-class membership and leftist allies, traditionally anti-militarist, are deeply dissatisfied.

@decrease_funding
subtitle: +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: ejercito_strength > 0
on-arrival: budget += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition = 1; prr_relation -= 8; ejercito_militancy -= 1; ejercito_strength -= 20; mf_strength += 15; rc_strength += 5; mf_militancy += 0.05; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.05 if ejercito_loyalty > 0; coup_progress += 1; coup_progress += 1 if ejercito_loyalty < 0.2; coup_progress += 1 if ejercito_loyalty < 0.1; coup_progress += 1 if ejercito_loyalty <= 0; reichswehr_goal_completed = 1; economic_growth -= 0.1

We slash military funds to balance our budget. While this frees up capital for social reform, it causes immense bitterness within the garrisons and officers' corps. 

Many demobilized or underpaid officers begin flirting openly with right-wing conspiratorial groups, and chatter of an impending *pronunciamiento* grows louder in the barracks.

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1 and ejercito_loyalty < 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the budget. ?][? if ejercito_loyalty >= 1 : The Ejército is already fully loyal to the democratic government. ?]
on-arrival: coalition_dissent -= 1; ejercito_loyalty += 0.15; ejercito_militancy -= 0.5 if ejercito_loyalty < 0.5; budget -= 1; coup_progress += 1; democratization += 1;

We overhaul the officer corps, offering generous pensions for hostile anti-republican generals to retire while promoting democratically-minded officers, althought many older liberal-minded officers have retired aswell. We also restructure military academies to modernize instruction.

While this reduces the immediate influence of reactionary generals inside active command, it alienates the conservative establishment and drives disgruntled retired officers directly into underground anti-republican plots.
